WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.969
-Our guests tonight are
three of my favorite people.

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.203
Please welcome back
to the show my family,

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:06.773
Hillary, Larry,
and Josh Meyers.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.808
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.166
Welcome back, everybody.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:36.102
-Year 10 of the tradition.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:38.437
-The tradition lives on.
-The tradition lives on.

00:00:38.437 --> 00:00:42.175
And it's very nice to have
you here in person, Dad.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:43.676
Last year, you were via Zoom

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:46.178
because you got a COVID
diagnosis right before you came.

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:47.614
And it worked out great.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:50.783
And, Mom, you said last year,
that was your favorite vibe.

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:53.386
-Yeah. I managed
to finish sentences.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.188
-You did.
That was the weird difference.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:56.889
Everybody was finishing
their own stories.

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:58.224
-Yeah.
-But I have to ask mom.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.659
-None of that tonight.
-None of that tonight.

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:02.028
-No mute button.
-Everything's cut off.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.729
But I want to ask --
This is a serious question.

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:05.532
Dad, you retired this year.
-Yes.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:08.401
-Congratulations.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.969
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:12.938
I am now part of
the gainfully unemployed.

00:01:12.938 --> 00:01:14.107
-Gainfully unemployed.

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.941
And, Mom,
that means he's in the house.

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:17.777
-Yes.
-And?

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.479
-Well, I nicknamed him
"Larry the Lurker."

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:22.715
-Larry the Lurker?
-Yeah.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.049
-He's doing a lot of lurking?

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:26.852
-No matter where I am,
he sneaks up behind me.

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:30.189
I go in a room,
he's in a corner, he jumps up.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:31.658
And you know
I have that startle reflex.

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:32.859
-Yeah.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:35.694
-That's why I'm doubting
he's actually jumping out

00:01:35.694 --> 00:01:37.630
in order to scare you.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:42.335
-It's amazing. She comes
into a room, and I'm there.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.537
-Yeah.
-That in itself is unnerving.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.473
-I live there,
and she comes into the room

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:50.576
and I'm maybe
coming out of a closet,

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:53.045
a bathroom, or something,
and she...

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:57.750
It's like so -- If Jimmy Hoffa

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.652
came out of the bathroom,
she would not be more surprised.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:00.986
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:03.756
-I mean, it's not a big house,
and you do live there,

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.291
so I feel like every room
you walk into,

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.627
there's like a 25% chance
he's going to be there.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.329
-There's a good shot
I'm there, yeah,

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.698
but she just is so shocked.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.499
-Yeah.
-It's unbelievable.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:15.835
-You're also not known
for your light footfalls.

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.536
-Yeah.
-Well...

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:19.705
-So I feel like
you could be able to track him

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.073
where he is in the house.

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:22.175
-He would have
to stand very still.

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:24.410
Dad is someone
where you just know --

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.245
And, by the way,
I have your footfalls, as well.

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:27.246
People know when we're coming.

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:28.380
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.216
-Well, the other thing is,
I have, you know,

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.851
a 100-pound sheepdog
that follows me everywhere I go.

00:02:32.851 --> 00:02:36.289
So if I go,
if a sheepdog walks into a room,

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:38.591
and she hasn't figured out
that I'm coming right after her,

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.859
or vice versa --

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:43.096
Yeah -- She's slow learner.
That's the problem.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:47.433
-I will say, you would make a
very bad detective, I feel like.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.602
-Well, yeah. You could be right.
-Yeah, I could be right.

00:02:50.602 --> 00:02:53.205
I will say that I just
came home a couple weeks ago,

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:54.807
and I always forget
that you guys

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.042
have a cardboard cutout of Josh.

00:02:57.042 --> 00:02:58.778
And when you open the door --
A life-size cutout.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:00.179
-Yeah.
-Sure.

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:03.983
-And, so, I am not -- I
will not blame myself for this,

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.417
but I opened the door,
and every time I walk in,

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:06.586
I'm like, "Oh [bleep]

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:09.888
Because when you walk in
and see your brother,

00:03:09.888 --> 00:03:13.026
who you know is not
in the state, just like this...

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.796
-You're not the only one
that happens to, by the way.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.230
Yeah.
-It was the best.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.799
It was a Mother's Day
present during the pandemic.

00:03:20.799 --> 00:03:22.535
-Yeah.
-So, there I am, all alone.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:25.104
Well, except for...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:30.509
And then, every time
I walk in the living room,

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:32.178
and I see Joshy waving to me.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:34.647
It's like I can go
on another day.

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.081
-And that was during
the pandemic, right?

00:03:36.081 --> 00:03:38.017
-That was the pandemic.
-And what did you give her?

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:40.320
-Mine got, like,
lost in the mail.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.155
-Yeah. Because that's why
we only have one cutout.

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:44.890
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
There's one cutout of Josh.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:49.295
I will say,
a two-cutout house is weird.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.797
That was big news --
you retired this year.

00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:54.033
The other big news --
Josh, congratulations.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.968
You got engaged.
-I did, I did.

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.403
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes, got engaged.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:58.738
-Thank you.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.674
Yeah.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:05.611
-How -- I was caught off guard.
-Yeah, you were.

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:08.447
-You and your a beautiful
fiancée FaceTimed me.

00:04:08.447 --> 00:04:10.649
And when you told me what
happened...

00:04:10.649 --> 00:04:11.985
-You cried right away.
-...I cried right away.

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.352
-Yep.

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:15.254
-And I mostly because I'm like,

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:18.991
"Oh, I don't want to have
to go to a wedding."

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:21.126
No, I really did cry.
I was very caught off guard.

00:04:21.126 --> 00:04:23.396
And how did it go down,
from your perspective?

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:26.799
-It was great. She's from
Shelburne Falls, Massachusetts.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.601
-A beautiful place.
-A beautiful little town

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.103
that has this bridge called
the Bridge of Flowers,

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:32.605
which has been
maintained for years

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:36.108
by the Shelburne Falls Area
Women's Club, all volunteers.

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:37.877
And it's this beautiful,
beautiful old

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:39.611
retired trolley bridge.

00:04:39.611 --> 00:04:41.814
And McKenzie suggested

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:44.449
we should walk across
the Bridge of Flowers.

00:04:44.449 --> 00:04:45.985
It's called the Bridge of
Flowers, if I didn't say that.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.454
And I was like,
"Oh, this is perfect.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.489
And I ran up.
I took a shower very quickly.

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:51.724
And she said,
"You took a shower?"

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.393
And I was like, "Yeah, I just --
I don't know.

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:55.294
I was sweaty.
I wanted to take a shower."

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:57.563
Ring in my pocket, and we walked
across the bridge.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.732
She crossed the bridge,
and then I was like,

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:02.035
"Oh, babe, there's a flower

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:04.403
I want you to see
over here in the middle."

00:05:04.403 --> 00:05:06.973
-That's a real good place to do
the "There's a flower" move.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.941
-Yeah, yeah.
Because I wasn't lying.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.043
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-I wasn't making it up.

00:05:10.043 --> 00:05:11.243
And, so, she walked past me,

00:05:11.243 --> 00:05:15.114
I, I guess, lurked behind her
for a moment.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.548
-It's genetic.
-It's genetic.

00:05:16.548 --> 00:05:17.984
You know how to do it.

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:20.953
-And then I tapped her on the
shoulder, and she turned around.

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:24.791
I took a knee.
She took a knee with me.

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:25.824
She was like,
"Now? This is happening now?

00:05:25.824 --> 00:05:26.959
It's happening here?"

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.327
And I said, "Yeah,
it's happening here."

00:05:28.327 --> 00:05:32.965
And, yeah, so, you know,
we sort of crouched down.

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:35.368
I said my piece.
I asked her to marry me.

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:37.636
She said, "I'm going
to have to think about it."

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:39.205
Then she said, "I'm kidding."

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:41.373
And I was like, "Well,
I would take a 'yes.'"

00:05:41.373 --> 00:05:44.176
Like, I'm not -- I'm gonna stay
down here until you say "yes."

00:05:44.176 --> 00:05:46.111
So she said "Yes."
-That's great.

00:05:46.111 --> 00:05:49.014
-And then we met up --
mom and dad were there.

00:05:49.014 --> 00:05:52.017
McKenzie's mom,
stepmom, and her dad --

00:05:52.017 --> 00:05:54.420
we all sort of got together
and had some champagne,

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.921
and it was --
Yeah, it was perfect.

00:05:55.921 --> 00:05:57.289
It's a beautiful story.

00:05:57.289 --> 00:06:00.592
And the other thing is,
I remember you told the story.

00:06:00.592 --> 00:06:01.660
You know,
we went to college together.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:02.761
We have the same
college friends,

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:03.829
and we were all together.

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:05.297
And you told this story about

00:06:05.297 --> 00:06:07.500
how you got -- you proposed
on the Bridge of Flowers,

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.635
and all our friends
wanted to ask was,

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.571
"Were you worried about bees?"

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:13.038
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.038 --> 00:06:15.875
-Well, it's also -- We kept it a
secret so that we could tell --

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:17.844
We had a big group trip
with all these guys,

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:20.012
and I was telling them --
Everyone else

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.948
in this group
of our friends is married.

00:06:21.948 --> 00:06:23.950
And so I was sort of saying,

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:26.218
I didn't want McKenzie
to feel bad on this trip

00:06:26.218 --> 00:06:28.287
because she's
the one girlfriend,

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:30.123
and everyone and our friends

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:34.026
thought I was about to propose
in our friend's kitchen at night

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.861
with people she had just met.

00:06:35.861 --> 00:06:39.265
And people went from
a state of, like, nausea

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:41.734
to when I said, "That's why
I proposed three days ago,

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:44.369
and she said 'yes'"
to just sweet relief.

00:06:44.369 --> 00:06:46.572
-Every one of our friends'
wives were thinking,

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:47.940
"Oh, God, not here."

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.109
-Yeah.
-It was really good.

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:51.677
So, it was very, very nice.

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:54.013
And you actually filmed a
video on The Bridge of Flowers,

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:56.249
which is a nice visual aid
for the story you just told.

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:58.183
This is the video
we all got from Josh.

00:06:58.183 --> 00:06:59.585
-In McKenzie's hometown,

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:03.656
there's this bridge called
the Bridge of Flowers.

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:05.357
Rightfully named.

00:07:05.357 --> 00:07:10.830
And we were out here the
other day and we got engaged.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.765
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:13.765 --> 00:07:15.300
-We love you guys so much.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.204
I'm gonna start
crying again now.

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:21.373
-Oh my God,
that is such a good video.

00:07:21.373 --> 00:07:23.509
When you sent it --
originally sent it,

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:25.011
I only watched the first
half of it, so it's --

00:07:25.011 --> 00:07:26.812
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah. Yeah.

00:07:26.812 --> 00:07:28.780
You've got that TikTok
sort of attention span.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:32.317
-But, also, I'm very excited.
McKenzie is here tonight.

00:07:32.317 --> 00:07:33.953
Can we see my soon-to-be
sister-in-law?

00:07:33.953 --> 00:07:35.454
There she is!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:35.454 --> 00:07:37.957
And her mother, Linda,
everybody.

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:42.561
Well, we've got a lot
more to talk about.

00:07:42.561 --> 00:07:43.962
It's been a big year.

00:07:43.962 --> 00:07:47.733
We will be right back with more
from the Meyers family.

